Rain.description:
Falling rain drawn as streaks around the camera. A singleton: the lowest entity id wins. The
drops live on a world-space lattice, so nothing swims when the camera moves, and they move with
game time. `intensity: 0` draws nothing and leaves the frame identical to a scene without it.

```
use ludion_components::Rain;

let rain: Rain = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "intensity": 0.5,
    "wind": [1.2, 0.0, 0.4],
}))
.unwrap();
assert_eq!(rain.density, 1.5);
assert_eq!(rain.fall_speed, [7.0, 9.0]);
```

RainOccluder.description:
Whether an entity's opaque meshes write the `rain_occlusion` map. Absent, a mesh occludes when it casts a
shadow. `{}` makes a non-caster occlude; `occludes: false` exempts a caster (a chain-link fence, a net
canopy). The nearest `RainOccluder` on the entity or a `Parent` ancestor wins. Blended and viewmodel
meshes never occlude.

```
use ludion_components::RainOccluder;

let net: RainOccluder = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "occludes": false })).unwrap();
assert!(!net.occludes);
assert!(serde_json::from_value::<RainOccluder>(serde_json::json!({})).unwrap().occludes);
```

RenderLayers.description:
Puts this entity, and every `Parent` descendant without its own `RenderLayers`, in the named
layers. An entity without one is in `default`. A `Camera.layers` or `RenderView.layers` list picks
which layers an image draws: meshes, sprites, ground markers, drop shadows, decals, particles and
world text, and their shadows.

```
use ludion_components::RenderLayers;

let layers: RenderLayers =
    serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "layers": ["radar"] })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(layers.layers, ["radar"]);
```

RenderView.description:
Renders the world through the `Camera` on this entity into its own texture of `size` texels, every
frame it is `enabled`, in the same frame. A `UiRect` shows it by naming it in `view`. A `Camera`
beside a `RenderView` is never the main camera. At most 4 enabled views render per frame.

```
use ludion_components::RenderView;

let view: RenderView = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "name": "radar" })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(view.size, [256, 256]);
assert!(view.enabled);
assert_eq!(view.order, 0);
assert!(view.sun && view.lights.is_none());
```

ScreenEffect.description:
A screen-look filter over the frame (`target: fill`) or a rectangle of it (`target: region`).
Drawn in UI order: elements with a lower `order` draw under it, the rest over it. Each stage is
optional; an unset stage takes the `preset`'s value, so the scene text carries only what was
overridden. An effect with every stage off is not applied. At most four are applied per frame
(`L2392`). Animated stages follow game time and `seed`.

```
use ludion_components::{ScreenEffect, ScreenEffectPreset};

let fx: ScreenEffect = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "preset": "crt",
    "scanlines": 0.5,
}))
.unwrap();
assert_eq!(fx.preset, ScreenEffectPreset::Crt);
assert_eq!(fx.stages().scanlines, 0.5);
assert_eq!(fx.stages().curvature, 0.06);
```

SightSampleRecord.description:
One carried sight sample of a [`Perceiver`] that is staggered or budgeted: what `perception_update`
last computed for `(perceiver, zone, target)`, kept while the perceiver is not evaluated. A runtime
entity, hashed and snapshotted, that despawns with its perceiver or when its key stops sampling.

```
use ludion_components::SightSampleRecord;

let record: SightSampleRecord = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "perceiver": { "index": 0, "generation": 0 }, "target": { "index": 1, "generation": 0 },
    "visible": true, "points_visible": 1, "distance": 4.0, "angle_deg": 10.0,
    "effective_range": 6.0, "evaluated_tick": 12,
}))
.unwrap();
assert!(record.visible && record.blocker.is_none() && record.in_zone);
```

SightPoint.description:
One place on a target a ray is cast to, and the layers that hide it.

```
use ludion_components::SightPoint;

let head: SightPoint = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "offset": [0.0, 1.6, 0.0], "blocked_by": ["wall", "cover_high"],
}))
.unwrap();
assert_eq!(head.blocked_by.as_slice(), ["wall", "cover_high"]);
```

LayerSet.description:
An ordered list of layer names, in the author's order (never sorted, so a scene's text does not
churn). Serializes as a plain list of strings.

```
use ludion_physics::LayerSet;

let set = LayerSet::from(vec!["light_occluder".to_string()]);
assert_eq!(set.as_slice(), ["light_occluder"]);
assert!(!set.is_empty());
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&set).unwrap(), r#"["light_occluder"]"#);
```

Require.description:
How many of a [`SightTarget`]'s sample points must be seen for the target to count as seen.

```
use ludion_components::Require;

let rule: Require = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "fraction": 0.5 })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(rule, Require::Fraction(0.5));
let all: Require = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!("all")).unwrap();
assert_eq!(all, Require::All);
```

StimulusRecord.description:
One thing a [`Perceiver`] sensed and still remembers: the ghost marker. `perception_update` and
`report_stimulus` write it; the game reads `last_position` of a record whose `sensed_now` is
`false` to search where the source was last seen. It is a runtime entity, hashed and snapshotted
like any other, and despawns with its perceiver or when forgotten.

```
use ludion_components::{Sense, StimulusRecord};

let record: StimulusRecord = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "perceiver": { "index": 0, "generation": 0 }, "sense": "sight", "last_position": [1.0, 0.0, 2.0],
    "first_sensed_tick": 10, "last_sensed_tick": 40,
}))
.unwrap();
assert_eq!(record.sense, Sense::Sight);
assert!(record.source.is_none() && !record.sensed_now);
```

Sense.description:
The channel a stimulus arrived on. Orders `sight`, `hearing`, then `custom` by number.

```
use ludion_components::Sense;

let custom: Sense = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "custom": 3 })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(custom, Sense::Custom(3));
assert!(Sense::Sight < Sense::Hearing && Sense::Hearing < custom);
```

SubtitleView.description:
A speaker-labelled, wrapped block of the dialogue lines on air, on a background panel.

It reads the engine's `Subtitles` list, so it draws only in a game that opts into dialogue; a
scene without a `SubtitleView` shows no subtitles. A game with its own look reads `Subtitles`
and omits the entity. An entity may carry a `Transform` alongside it; it is ignored.

```
use ludion_components::SubtitleView;

let view: SubtitleView = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "anchor": "bottom_center",
    "max_lines": 2,
    "channels": ["radio", "ui"],
}))
.unwrap();
assert_eq!(view.max_lines, 2);
assert_eq!(view.size, 30.0);
```

UiGroup.description:
A screen-space box that other UI elements anchor inside, scale, fade and hide as one unit. It
draws nothing: it resolves like a [`UiRect`](crate::UiRect) (`anchor`, `offset`, `size`), and a
`UiRect`, `UiText`, `UiList` or another `UiGroup` with `group: <this entity>` anchors against that
box instead of the canvas. `scale` (about the box centre), `opacity` and `visible: false` compose
onto every descendant through nesting of up to 8 groups. `order` stays global; a group never
reorders its children. `UiTween` (offset, size, scale, opacity) and `UiWorldAnchor` work on a
group.

```yaml
components:
  UiGroup: { anchor: top_right, offset: [-24, 24], size: [360, 360], opacity: 0.9 }
```

```
use ludion_components::UiGroup;

let group: UiGroup = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({})).unwrap();
assert_eq!(group, UiGroup::default());
assert_eq!(group.size, [100.0, 100.0]);
assert!(group.visible);
```

UiClipShape.description:
The shape a [`UiGroup`] clips its descendants to, externally tagged: `clip: rect`,
`clip: circle` (the circle inscribed in the group's box) or
`clip: { rounded_rect: { corner_radius: 12.0 } }` (canvas units, `>= 0`).

```
use ludion_components::UiClipShape;

let clip: UiClipShape = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!("rect")).unwrap();
assert_eq!(clip, UiClipShape::Rect);
assert!(UiClipShape::default().is_none());
```

TextOutline.description:
An outline drawn under the glyphs of a [`UiText`](crate::UiText) or [`UiList`]. A `width` of `0`,
or a `color` alpha of `0`, draws nothing.

```
use ludion_components::TextOutline;

let outline: TextOutline =
    serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "width": 2.0, "color": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0] })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(outline.width, 2.0);
```

TextShadow.description:
A copy of the text's ink (the fill, plus the outline when there is one) drawn under it, moved by
`offset`. A `color` alpha of `0` draws nothing.

```
use ludion_components::TextShadow;

let shadow: TextShadow = serde_json::from_value(
    serde_json::json!({ "offset": [2.0, 2.0], "color": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.6] }),
)
.unwrap();
assert_eq!(shadow.softness, 0.0);
```

UiRadial.description:
A tool wheel: up to 16 items on a ring, the selected one chosen by aim. Screen space, like
[`UiList`](crate::UiList): it shares `UiRect`'s 1080-unit canvas and pivot rule, over a square box
`2 * radius_outer` wide, so the wheel centre is the box centre.

Angles are clock degrees: 0 is 12 o'clock and positive is clockwise. Item `i` is centred at
`start_deg + i * 360 / n`. [`navigate`](UiRadial::navigate) moves `selected` and `pointer`, the only
fields it writes, and reports an activation as its return value.

```
use ludion_components::{UiRadial, UiRadialItem};

let radial: UiRadial = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "items": [{ "text": "AXE" }, { "text": "BOW" }]
})).unwrap();
assert_eq!(radial.radius_outer, 220.0);
assert_eq!(radial.selected, None);
```

TextOutline.description:
An outline drawn under the glyphs of a [`UiText`](crate::UiText) or [`UiList`]. A `width` of `0`,
or a `color` alpha of `0`, draws nothing.

```
use ludion_components::TextOutline;

let outline: TextOutline =
    serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "width": 2.0, "color": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0] })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(outline.width, 2.0);
```

UiSlice.description:
A nine-slice frame for a textured [`UiRect`](crate::UiRect): the corners keep their size, the
edges stretch along one axis and the centre stretches or is hidden.

```
use ludion_components::ui::{UiSlice, UiSliceCenter};

let slice: UiSlice = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({ "border": [4, 4, 4, 4] })).unwrap();
assert_eq!(slice.scale, 1.0);
assert_eq!(slice.center, UiSliceCenter::Stretch);
```

UiShape.description:
An analytic screen-space shape: one SDF-drawn primitive with a fill and a stroke. Screen space, like
[`UiRect`](crate::UiRect): the 1080-unit canvas, `anchor` + `offset`, `group`, `UiTween` and
`UiWorldAnchor`.

The shape's local `(0, 0)` sits at the anchor point plus `offset`; scale and `rotation` pivot there,
not on a bounds centre. `line` and `arc` draw only their `stroke`; the other kinds draw `fill`,
`stroke` or both. A shape with neither draws nothing.

```
use ludion_components::{UiShape, UiShapeType};

let shape: UiShape = serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
    "shape": { "type": "ring", "radius": 40, "thickness": 6, "sweep_deg": 270 },
    "fill": [1, 1, 1, 1]
})).unwrap();
assert!(matches!(shape.shape, UiShapeType::Ring { sweep_deg, .. } if sweep_deg == 270.0));
```

